; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 26 drum-kit records x 295 bytes: 16-char display name + 279 parameter bytes.
; Kits 0-13 are the first bank (Standard..MSP), kits 14-25 the second bank
; (Standard..Sound Effect).  Only ~19 parameter bytes differ between kits;
; per-note instrument assignment lives in DrumKit_NoteMapA/B (below), whose
; entries index the PercInst_* records.
;
; RECORD LAYOUT, FROM THE READERS (2026-09-25).  A kit is a tone record whose
; +0x10 byte has bits 7:6 = 10: Voice_SetVelocity (subcpu 0x02C8E4) switches on
; tonerec[+0x10] & 0xC0 and sends mode 0x80 to Voice_SetVelocity_Type80_Entry
; (0x02CB93) -> Voice_NoteOn_Type1 (0x02C2C0), which allocates the two layers of
; the note's drum instrument (see the PercInst header below).
;   +0x00  16-char name
;   +0x10  0x80 in all 26 (part mode 0x80)
;   +0x11  0, 2, 3, 4, 5 or 6 -- no reader found
;   +0x12..+0x26  identical in all 26 kits -- no reader found
;   +0x27  128 x {wave byte, slot byte}, entry n = MIDI note n (the C that
;          Voice_SetVelocity passes on as Voice_NoteOn_Type1's E = key).  For
;          note n ToneDB_Find_SubToneRecord (0x032AE0) reads rec[0x27+2n] and
;          rec[0x28+2n], and ToneDB_Resolve_NamedToneRecord (0x032A08) turns
;          them into  PercInst = dir[+0x78] + dir.u16[+0xEE]
;                        * u16[dir[+0x74] + 2*(((slot & 0x1F) << 7) | (wave & 0x7F))]
;          = DrumKit_NoteMapA[slot][wave].  Slot bit 5 would select a RAM (user)
;          record instead; it is clear in all 3,328 kit entries.
;   The row comments name the drum instrument each note resolves to ("-" =
;   Silent).  Cross-check: the name copier DSP_SetVoiceCoefficients (0x03111A)
;   resolves the same pair through DrumKit_NoteMapB into PercName_Pack, and
;   the two names agree on 3236 of 3328 notes (the rest differ only in
;   numbering, e.g. "Scratch 3" / "Scratch 2", or "Zap 1" / "High Q").
;   Kits 14-17, 19 and 20 (bank selector 0x41) put hi-hats on notes 42/46 and
;   a crash on 49, the General MIDI layout; no bank-0x40 kit does.
;   Reproduce: python3 notes/tonedb-2026-09-25/drum_chain_probe.py
; Drum kit 00 "Standard Kit": tone number 315, chosen by bank sel 0x40 prog 0, sel 0x40 prog 15.
; Part mode 0x80 (Voice_SetVelocity); note n -> PercInst via the pair at +0x27+2n (see header).
DrumKit_00_StandardKit:
	.ascii	"  Standard Kit  "
	.byte	0x80									; +0x10 part mode 0x80 = drum kit
	.byte	0x02									; +0x11 varies 0..6 across kits; no reader found
	.byte	0x55, 0x81, 0x40, 0xff, 0x03, 0x40, 0x55, 0x00, 0x40, 0x55, 0x00, 0x40, 0x55, 0x00, 0x40, 0x55, 0x00, 0x40, 0x55, 0x00, 0x40	; +0x12..+0x26 identical in all 26 kits
