; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 610 percussion-instrument records x 58 bytes (dir +0x78).
; Record: 13-char name, 3 header bytes, then two 21-byte layer parameter
; blocks.  The two layers are byte-identical in 609 of 610 records (the
; exception is flagged below).  DrumKit_NoteMapA/B entries index this table;
; PercName_Pack (0x87D322) also has exactly 610 entries.
;
; READERS (2026-09-25).  For each drum note Voice_NoteOn_Type1 (subcpu
; 0x02C2C0) calls Voice_Allocate_Type2 (0x02C12B) twice, for layer 0 with
; DE = 1 and layer 1 with DE = 4.  It resolves this record through the kit
; (DrumKit header above), stores it in the voice slot at +0x13, and:
;   +0x0D  LAYER MASK: layer L is refused unless (rec[+0x0D] & DE) != 0, so
;          bit 0 = layer 0, bit 2 = layer 1.  Census 0x01 x540, 0x21 x69,
;          0x25 x1 -- record 452, the only one with a second layer and the
;          only one whose two layer blocks differ.  Bit 5 switches the voice
;          to a fixed level: Voice_WriteVolume_OrPan (0x026C16) and
;          Voice_Calc_LevelPair_FixedAtk (0x025A35) test it.
;   +0x0E  0x00 x608, 0x40 x2; +0x0F seven values -- no reader found for either
;   +0x10 + 0x15*L  LAYER L, 21 bytes: the voice slot's paramA (slot +0x17,
;          Voice_Allocate_Type2: rec + 0x10 + 0x15*layer).
; LAYER fields with a reader (paramA+N; code re-read 2026-09-25):
;   +0x01, +0x02  wave-select pair -> WaveSel_StageA1_FromToneSlot (0x032682)
;   +0x05  channel detune: +(value - 0x64), or a fixed -0x200 when 0
;          (Voice_ApplyPortamento2, 0x026684)
;   +0x06  signed detune, +0x07 pitch-curve selector, 0xE0 = the direct note
;          table 0x011C96 (Voice_ComputePitch_Mono, 0x026533)
;   +0x08  segment-0 target, +0x0E its key scale; +0x09/+0x0A segment-1
;          target/rate; +0x0B/+0x0C segment-2 target/rate (amplitude
;          envelope, Voice_Calc_LevelPair_FixedAtk)
;   +0x0D  the fixed level used when rec[+0x0D] bit 5 is set
;          (Voice_WriteVolume_OrPan)
; +0x00, +0x03, +0x04 (0 in all 610) and +0x0F..+0x14 have no reader found.
; Each record's header says which kit notes play it.
