; READERS (2026-09-25): these are TONE RECORDS, tone numbers 336 (Jazz) and 337
; (Rock) of ToneDB_ToneOffsetTable, chosen through bank selector 0x70
; (ToneDB_ToneNumBank_Main10: program 1 -> 337, every other program -> 336).
; Byte +0x10 = 0x60, so Voice_SetVelocity (subcpu 0x02C8E4) takes part mode
; 0x40 (tonerec[+0x10] & 0xC0) -> Voice_SetVelocity_Type40_Entry ->
; Voice_NoteOn_Type2 (4 voice slots).  +0x11 = 0x01 is the partial mask; for a
; bank selector >= 0x10 VoiceBuf_TypeSelector_MatchEpilogue (0x032082) tests only
; partial 0 against it and binds partials 1-3 to blocks 1-3 unpacked, and these
; records do carry all four partial blocks (426 = 21 + 5*81).  The drawbar zone records
; they end up selecting are DrawbarPreset_EnvData_* below.  The parenthesis
; above ("drawbar footage levels, percussion/click settings") is not tied to
; any byte by a reader.
